    "status": "published",
    "content": "FSSAI’s Hygiene Rating Scheme was introduced so that diners can make informed choices about where they eat — and so that food businesses have a clear reason to showcase and improve their hygiene standards.\n\n## How the rating works\n\nFood service establishments are rated on a scale of **1 to 5**, shown as smileys, where 5 indicates excellent compliance with food hygiene and safety requirements. The rating is awarded by an FSSAI-recognised third-party audit agency after assessing the outlet against a hygiene rating checklist. A certificate is generated and should be displayed prominently in the customer-facing area of your premises.\n\nThe rating reflects the hygiene standards found on the date of inspection — so consistent day-to-day practice matters.\n\n## Who should get rated\n\nThe scheme is aimed at businesses that serve food directly to consumers, such as:\n\n- Restaurants and hotels\n- Cafes and quick-service outlets\n- Cloud kitchens\n- Bakeries and sweet shops\n- Caterers and food courts\n\n## How to prepare\n\n1. Make sure your food business is licensed or registered with FSSAI.\n2. Carry out a self-assessment against the hygiene rating checklist and fix the gaps.\n3. Check staff hygiene, cleaning schedules, pest control, storage temperatures and records.\n4. Schedule the audit with a recognised audit agency.\n\n## Why it is worth doing\n\nA visible hygiene rating builds trust with customers in your restaurant and on food-delivery platforms, gives your kitchen team a clear improvement checklist, and helps demonstrate compliance during inspections.",
